## Non-blocking follow-ups

- **`ScopeId` in clause-ir** — already landed in R1; BACKLOG
  only notes that any future cross-crate tweak should stay
  reusable.
- **String interning for `Symbol` names** — replace owned
  `String` with an interned handle; halves memory on large
  workspaces and makes `Symbol` `Copy`.
- **Incremental resolve for IDE** — delta walk that re-resolves
  only the changed subtree, keyed off AST node diff.

## Diagnostic surface

- `ResolveError` currently carries two variants
  (`UnresolvedIdentifier`, `DuplicateDefinition`); additional
  variants (`AmbiguousImport`, `CycleDetected`, `PrivateAccess`,
  `UnknownCrate`) arrive with the rule that first emits them.
- `ManifestError` currently carries two variants (`Parse`,
  `NotImplemented`); real TOML parsing will extend this with
  `MissingField`, `InvalidVersion`, `DuplicateDependency`, etc.
- The `From<ResolveError> for Diagnostic` conversion currently
  emits static placeholder messages; follow-up rounds replace
  them with per-variant messages once the producer rules land.

## Front-end review notes

- **`ResolveError` is not `Copy`** because
  `UnresolvedIdentifier.name` and `DuplicateDefinition.name` hold
  owned `String`. This breaks the `E: Copy + Into<Diagnostic>`
  symmetry that the rest of the front-end preserves
  (`SyntaxError` is `Copy`; `Diagnostic` is `Copy`). The fix
  lands naturally with the Symbol-interning round listed under
  "Non-blocking follow-ups" above: once `Symbol::name` is an
  `InternedSymbol` (or similar small `Copy` handle), the two
  `ResolveError` variants become `Copy` at no extra cost and
  `ResolveError` itself becomes `Copy`. Do not try to work
  around the issue before the interning round lands — the
  owned `String` is load-bearing while names are raw strings,
  and short-term workarounds (e.g. splitting the enum into
  `Copy` and non-`Copy` halves) create more surface than they
  save.
